these have identified the two women they  say were involved in a crash that killed  two toddlers that happened in North Las  Vegas we thank you for joining us on 8  news now at 11 I'm Brian Loftis officers  say the children's aunt was behind the  wheel Under the Influence when she hit a  tree head on their mother riding in the  passenger seat this all happened near  Lone Mountain and Simmons it happened on  Sunday night Sasha Loftus spoke directly  with family tonight joins us live at the  crash site now Sasha with more  Brian this is the spot where that deadly  crash happened here in North Las Vegas  you can see a memorial is still standing  where those two girls were killed the  woman I spoke with Tonight is their  great grandmother on their father's side  she said as horrible as this is she  wants others to learn from the tragedy  they were two beautiful girls Wilma  Wilmer shares her sadness over the  sudden loss of her two  great-granddaughters they were smart  two-year-old Rose Wilmer and  three-year-old Taylor Wilmer were killed  in a violent crash Sunday night  here near Lone Mountain and Simmons in  North Las Vegas  police say 25-year-old Kalia Manning  identified as the toddler's aunt was  driving Under the Influence when she  lost control of the car and hit a tree  head-on the children's Mother 23 year  old rhonisa Washington was riding in the  passenger seat and is facing child  endangerment charges this is a call to  action  about DUI speed and proper child  restraints in a news conference earlier  this week North Las Vegas Police shared  that neither child had proper safety  restraints and says this led to Rose  being decapitated I was hoping that this  tragedy could bring light to people  about buckling up their children in  proper restraints Wilmer tells me while  her family tries to cope with this  unimaginable loss she hopes their story  can serve as a wake-up call for others  on the road don't want their death to be  in vain  now records show the child's mother was  also charged with felony domestic  battery in Henderson back in November  now as for Manning the woman who was  driving the car at the time of this  crash she faces multiple charges  including three counts of DUI resulting  in death or substantial bodily harm  reporting live in North Las Vegas  tonight Sasha Loftus 8 News Now
 

